# Pin line endings + binary classification for the Pythia CAS-probe
# research artifacts (Codex audit 37d0a62 finding 2). The manifest's
# sha256 of the snapshot must be reproducible on any host, including
# Windows checkouts that would otherwise translate LF → CRLF on `git
# checkout`.

# Treat all research JSON/JSONL as text but force LF line endings so the
# on-disk bytes match the sha256 recorded in the manifest.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# Numpy .npz files are binary archives — never apply EOL conversion.
*.npz binary
